      "title": "Netanyahu reportedly pressured military to attack Iran in run-up to election",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/netanyahu-reportedly-pressured-israel-military-attack-iran-runup-to-election",
      "description": "<p>Israeli prime minister increases alarmist rhetoric as his far-right coalition narrowly trails in polls</p><p>Benjamin Netanyahu has resorted to increasingly alarmist rhetoric and reportedly put pressure on Israel’s military to take action against Iran as his far-right coalition narrowly trails in the polls ahead of Tuesday’s close-run elections.</p><p>The Israeli prime minister posted an AI-generated image of a nuclear mushroom cloud destroying Tel Aviv, telling Israeli voters to choose him or risk nuclear annihilation.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/netanyahu-reportedly-pressured-israel-military-attack-iran-runup-to-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
